To find the total number of times Chase and Rider ride their bikes a week, we first calculate the number of times they ride on the usual days. They ride thrice a day for 5 days, so \(3 \times 5 = 15\) times. On the two other days, they ride twice the usual times, so \(2 \times 15 = 30\) times. Adding these together gives \(15 + 30 = 45\) times per week.

